{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall regard them as uncircumcised.</b> This verse speaks of a child: three years it shall be to you as uncircumcised — when he does not know how to speak; and in the fourth year you shall eat its fruit — for then he begins to read in the Torah; and from there onward, to add to you its produce — as the Sages, blessed be their memory, said: from here onward you accept him like a bull. From here the Sages said: at five years for Scripture, at ten for Mishnah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:19.269624961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}